  "releaseNotes": "LC045 now reports a foreach directly over a query widened to IEnumerable<T>. IEnumerable<Order> source = db.Orders; foreach (var o in source) runs the query exactly as iterating db.Orders does, and the same loop over source.ToList() was already reported. The chain proof decides it rather than the declared type, so a plain List, a LINQ-to-objects query and a reassigned local stay quiet. The 5.7.32 code fix already covers the shape.",
